{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Regularity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Regularity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.Jacobian","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Complex","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Lebesgue.Complex","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.BumpFunction.Normed","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.BumpFunction.InnerProduct","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Convolution","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Inv","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Algebra"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.contDiffOn_of_fiveTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.contDiffOn_of_fiveTerm","kind":"theorem","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L343-L418","doc":"**Stage R.** A solution of the five-term relation that is continuous on `{0,1}ᶜ` and\ninversion-odd is `C^∞` on `{0,1}ᶜ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.contDiffOn_of_fiveTerm_core","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.contDiffOn_of_fiveTerm_core","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L187-L341","doc":"**Regularity core.** Let `φ` be continuous on `{0,1}ᶜ`, inversion-odd and satisfying\nthe five-term relation.  Let `X, Y` be compact, with `X, Y ⊆ {0,1}ᶜ` and `X ∩ Y = ∅`, let\n`ψ` be smooth with `∫ ψ = 1`, vanishing off `Y` and off `‖y‖ ≤ M`.  Then `φ` is smooth on any\nopen `s ⊆ X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.mem_U","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.mem_U","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L183-L185","doc":"Membership in `{0,1}ᶜ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.contDiff_invKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.contDiff_invKernel","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L161-L181","doc":"`Ψ(w) = ‖w⁻¹‖⁴ ψ(w⁻¹)` is smooth on all of `ℂ` when `ψ` is smooth and vanishes\noutside a bounded set avoiding `0`: near `w = 0` it is identically zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.integrable_of_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.integrable_of_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L151-L159","doc":"A continuous-on-`Y` integrand that vanishes off a compact `Y` is integrable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.contDiff_normSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.contDiff_normSq","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L146-L149","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.contDiffOn_integral_kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.contDiffOn_integral_kernel","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L112-L144","doc":"An integral against a smooth, parameter-dependent kernel with fixed compact support\n`k` is smooth in the parameter, for any `φ` continuous on a neighbourhood of `k`.\n(Mathlib's convolution-with-parameter theorem, evaluated at `0`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.integral_comp_inv_one_sub_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.integral_comp_inv_one_sub_mul","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L77-L110","doc":"`∫ F(y) dy = ∫ ‖c/(1−ct)²‖² F((1 − c t)⁻¹) dt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.integral_comp_one_sub_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.integral_comp_one_sub_mul","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L66-L75","doc":"`∫ F(y) dy = ‖c‖² ∫ F(1 − c t) dt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.integral_comp_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.integral_comp_mul","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L55-L64","doc":"`∫ F(y) dy = ‖x‖² ∫ F(x t) dt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.integral_eq_compl_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.integral_eq_compl_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L50-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.integral_image_holo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.integral_image_holo","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L37-L48","doc":"Change of variables along a holomorphic map, injective on `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.det_mul_eq_normSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.det_mul_eq_normSq","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Regularity.lean#L28-L35","doc":"The real determinant of multiplication by `c` on `ℂ` is `‖c‖²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}